@nfcampos is there a good way to associate the name of a tool (e.g., from a tool call) to a task?

One option is something like
```python
def _make_task_from_tool(tool):

    @task
    def tool_task(tool_call):
        observation = tool.invoke(tool_call)
        return ToolMessage(content=observation, tool_call_id=tool_call["id"])

    tool_task.__wrapped__.__name__ = tool.name
    return tool_task
```

@vbarda I wanted to bring this to your attention: this change was introduced in a new release as a minor update (changing only the last digit of the version). However, it actually constitutes a breaking change since it requires inheriting from another class when using structured responses.

Given its impact, I believe it would be beneficial to refine the release process to better account for these kinds of changes. This would help ensure smoother transitions for users relying on the current implementation.

